        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Anhaica, Tallahassee, Florida\n- People: Apalachee\n- Languages: Apalachee, Muskogean languages\n- Topics: Alternate names, extinction\n\nFacts:\n- Anhaica, also known as Iviahica, Yniahico, and the pueblo of Apalache, was the principal town of the Apalachee people.\n- Anhaica was located in what is now Tallahassee, Florida.\n- The Apalachee people spoke the Apalachee language.\n- The Apalachee language was a Muskogean language.\n- The Apalachee language is now extinct.",
